# Obsidian vault in this repo

Personal notes live in `Obsidian Vault/` (vault name: **Obsidian Vault**). Treat them as the user's knowledge base, not application source.

## How to access notes

- Read and edit the `.md` files on disk. Wikilink `[[Note Name]]` maps to a file named `Note Name.md` (search the vault if it is nested).
- Do **not** rely on `obsidian://open?...` URIs. That scheme only opens inside the Obsidian app; agents cannot follow it.
- Index / home note: `Obsidian Vault/Home.md`. Leave `.obsidian/` config alone unless the user asks to change Obsidian settings.
- Keep markdown Obsidian-compatible (wikilinks, YAML frontmatter). Prefer updating existing notes over creating duplicates.
- Do not commit secrets from notes. Do not dump the whole vault into a reply; cite the relevant note instead.

## One fact, one note

Each fact has exactly one **owner** note. Write it there. Everywhere else, only `[[wikilink]]`.

- Meeting note in `Toplantı Notları/` — owns what was said in that meeting. Never copy another meeting into it.
- Concept note (`DWH`, `Kale`, `ODS`, `PowerDesigner`, …) — owns the durable definition of that thing.
- `Fiziksel Topoloji - Teknik Taraf` — owns environments, databases, tooling.
- `Aktif Sorular` — owns open questions. Other notes link here instead of restating a question.
- `Proje Planı` — owns plan and action items. `Home.md` — index only.

 Treat the vault as one notebook.
